expeditions/2026-06-20-aoyagi-full/lessons.md:1265:I briefed seambuild to `git checkout -B genm-seam` — but `origin/genm-seam` already existed (geleg8's old `schurReadout_germ_eq_gen` seam, since integrated/stale). seambuild's diverging local `genm-seam` couldn't push without a non-fast-forward failure or a force-push over the live stale ref. Extends the #67 explicit-unique-WORKTREE-path lesson to BRANCH NAMES: before handing a tide a branch name, `git for-each-ref refs/remotes/origin/<name>` (or ls-remote) to confirm it's free — expedition branch names collide easily because tides reuse topical stems ("seam", "geleg", "hstep2"). Fix when it happens: redirect the tide to push `HEAD:<distinct-name>` (banking keeps the local worktree; only the remote name changes) — never force over the colliding ref. Cost this time: near-zero (caught before seambuild pushed).
expeditions/2026-06-20-aoyagi-full/lessons.md:1291:vsastruct's (decorrelated, sound) corank2-cert proposed an analytic Architecture for the (3,3,3,4) deep strata: front-first coupled majorant → two-block radial → tube; cover = top stratum (LAYER 2) + deep strata (corner). I commissioned + banked on it (crux `twoBlock_radial_le` @56125ea9, `FrontSpectral` @cdd0b206, + 2 in-flight tides) — THEN ran the self-recon on the (S,J) endpoint. The recon (VERIFIED vs live code) revealed the LIVE (A)-native route is a DIFFERENT, more-banked architecture: the **decorated recursion** `DecoratedPeelStep` (Schur-split not Gram-spectral; `radialAttach`-across-levels not a 2-scale brick; corner atom + terminal + charge bookkeeping ALL already banked), gap = T4/T2a′/T5. The cert's route was a valid PARALLEL derivation whose hardest piece (the deep tube) routes back into the native corner anyway. Cost: 2 banked lemmas + review cycles on a parallel route (kept — correct+reusable — but off the native critical path); 2 tides stood down (caught before they wrote files, ~zero loss).
