expeditions/2026-06-20-aoyagi-full/discuss-at-close.md:2816:Two decorrelated passes (a self-recon that mapped the LIVE banked code, then a vsastruct pen-and-paper adjudication) converged the route and located the true crux. Recording the shape for your return; still no wall, still within the (A) build. **What resolved:** (1) The live (A)-native (□)-gate is a SINGLE unproven `Prop` `DecoratedPeelStep` (`RouteMSJDecoratedRec.lean:78`) — its driver already proves, sorry-free, `DecoratedPeelStep → (□)` AND `→` the exact old `sjJointResolution:803` goal (so `:803` is obsolete; I verified this against the code). The corner blow-up atom, the terminal, the radial peel, the charge bookkeeping, the Schur-split/shear are ALL banked. So (□) reduces to proving this one Prop. (2) The vsastruct-cert "front-first majorant / stratified cover" Architecture (on which I'd banked the crux `twoBlock_radial_le` + `FrontSpectral`) is a PARALLEL route the live code doesn't use — I pivoted to the native decorated recursion (those two banks stay, correct+reusable, off the native critical path; lesson recorded: recon the live architecture before committing to a cert's Architecture). **The true crux (decorrelated-confirmed):** proving `DecoratedPeelStep` is NOT a single peel onto the plain box IH — the banked corner atom emits a persistent `det(Q_bQ_bᵀ)^{−a/2}` coupling that is genuine extra weight the plain IH can't absorb (a 4-node peel lands on a 3-node *decorated* integral). It is the honest **decorated double induction** (carry the det/minor weight through a decorated IH), ~65–75% genuinely-new content — the same figure every prior pass flagged, now located precisely. **Not a wall:** the true integral is finite at 7/2 (three independent ways); the decbuild carrier (`SJDecoration`/`DecoratedBoxThresholdFinite`) was built to carry exactly this weight. **The soundness crux (your close-time check):** the det valuation and the reduced loss share the deeper A₂-rank-drop divisor; the resolution must ADD their charges (→7/2), never MIN (→ the `z²(x²+y²)` RLCT-collapse, 3/2) — and the "a.e. in A'" framing is a red flag (unbounded weight near a null set), so the tube must be resolved explicitly-stratified, not ignored. This is the conceptual-slop trap; the T4 build's close will gate on a decorrelated check that the charge-addition (not min) is faithful. **Status:** vsastruct producing the definitive T4 design cert (decorated-IH double induction vs standalone anisotropic lemma; the exact strengthened predicate + what's already banked in the carrier vs new); the T4 formaliser waits on it. **No action needed** — flagged so that at close you can sanity-check the (□)-discharge genuinely ADDED the shared-divisor charges (didn't min-split / RLCT-collapse), and that `DecoratedPeelStep` (or its strengthened form) is proved with the honest decorated IH.
expeditions/2026-06-20-aoyagi-full/discuss-at-close.md:2819:Execution on the (□)-core (`DecoratedPeelStep`) is underway; two decorrelated-reviewed pieces are banked, and the architecture simplified vs the design phase's worry. **Banked:** (1) `corner334` (@96409822) — the fixed-A₂ corner SLICE: the **min→sum mechanism validated in Lean** (indicator-`prependColumn` → the additive corner → 7/2 via a banked weighted-AM-GM endpoint; NOT the 3/2 multiplicative `radialAttach`), + the sharp divergence boundary; (2) `onePeel334` (@a39a37e4) — the (3,3,3,4) one-peel finiteness at 7/2 in **clean coordinates**, with the A₂-rank-drop complement **rescued by codimension** (a Morse integral, non-binding), genuinely closed. **The design simplified:** the A₂-rank-drop is a Morse codim-rescue, NOT a deeper (S,J) recursion (UPDATE-880) — the feared deeper-stratum dissolves; the add-vs-min RLCT-collapse trap lives inside the sector slice (banked correct). Each piece survived controller-review + a decorrelated reviewer + the vsastruct architect-audit (the corner334 round caught + fixed a false-premise "cover" my review had passed — the decorrelated discipline is load-bearing and working). **Remaining to the literal (3,3,3,4) `DecoratedPeelStep` body:** the A₂-casting (a det-M≠0 constant-Jacobian CoV — load-bearing, being scoped) + the chart tie-back (pivot+Schur+shear → the corner-slice structure) — both buildable-as-labour; then the admissible class + decorated driver + `m>2` for the general recursion. **For close (no action now):** a checkpoint that the (□)-core is being built piece-by-piece, each decorrelated-reviewed + honestly scope-named (`_slice`/`_cleanCoords_` mark the exact object proved, not the aspiration).
expeditions/2026-06-20-aoyagi-full/discuss-at-close.md:2826:Surfacing a real index-honesty finding (no action needed; recording the lesson + how I'm handling it). While scoping the §5 lane's B5-desc majorant fill (GAP-B), I found that **task #112 (`det_le_det_of_posSemidef_le` + `det_submatrix_sq_le_det_gram`, the PSD-cone det-monotonicity + Gram-minor bound) is NOT recoverable.** #112 was marked "completed / banked" but its note said "banked on genm-cbmin **worktree branch**, integrate at final consolidation" — that branch was never integrated to canonical nor pushed to origin, and is now gone: `git branch -a` has no cbmin ref, and a `git log --all -S` across all history finds the lemma in ZERO `.lean` files (only in synthesis/thread docs). The MATH is certified (in the docs); the LEAN is lost. It's also not in Mathlib. So the majorant fill must REBUILD the det-monotonicity (genm-sj5-schur, in GAP-B) — modest labour (it's a clean "Mathlib-worthy" PSD lemma), and the de-risk needs the m-column form anyway (not #112's single-minor, which reached only a<1). **Two lessons:** (1) **"banked on a worktree branch" ≠ banked** — worktree branches must be integrated to canonical OR pushed to origin before the worktree is cleaned, else the work evaporates (flip side of the #100 INFRA item). (2) An honest index must distinguish *banked-in-canonical* from *certified-in-a-thread-doc* — I've corrected BUILT-INDEX (the "#112 BANKED" claim → "#112 LOST, rebuild"). Net cost: a small rebuild, not a wall. Flagging so the pattern gets a harness-level guard if it recurs.
expeditions/2026-06-20-aoyagi-full/discuss-at-close.md:2832:A clean strategic resolution of the two-lane structure you set up, worth your eye. Both lanes' fill has reduced to a SINGLE shared brick: `g(Q) = ∫_{A₀} frobSq(A₀·Q)^{−c'} ≤ C·σ_q(Q)^{−α}` (the front-first box-exponent bound). Lane 1 (#121, native cover/σ_min) needs g(Q) directly; the §5 lane (#125) needs recombine (banked) + g(Q) + tube (banked) — so g(Q) is the ONLY un-banked brick for either. **The §5 lane's payoff, concretely:** it banked EVERYTHING else (the skeleton/recombine/tube/#127/det-monotone) and ISOLATED g(Q) as the sole remaining brick. So "attack the heart directly" (your directive) succeeded exactly as intended — it didn't avoid the hard core, it *isolated* it and banked all the scaffolding around it. **The hard core = the sector-from-region bridge** (`RouteMSJFrontSpectral` 3iii+3ii, held since UPDATE-869): the front-first bound goes through a dominance SECTOR, and deriving that sector on the right region (+ covering the box by sectors + measurability) is the "structure adjudication" — RED-FLAGGED by secinfra F2 (the sector does NOT follow naively from dominance). This is the irreducible analytic core of the entire (□); vsastruct did substantial prior work on it (the rank-dichotomy, the corank-2 coupled majorant, c'<7/2), but the sector derivation is the held piece. **Plan:** build g(Q) ONCE (shared, both lanes consume it) — the conditional part (given the sector) is buildable now (~80-120 LoC, genm-sj5-schur); the sector-from-region crux is being de-risked (genm-sj5-cover, consuming vsastruct + dodging F2, decorrelated). **The fork this sets up (for your awareness, not yet forced):** if the sector-from-region is bounded labour → (□) closes and the unsuffixed `aoyagi_learning_coefficient` is mintable; if the F2 sector⇍dominance concern is a genuine obstruction → that is the one real wall of the whole programme, and I'll surface it with the decorrelated witness. The cert is in flight; no action needed — flagging that the discharge has narrowed to its true core.
expeditions/2026-06-20-aoyagi-full/discuss-at-close.md:2844:A fidelity-critical finding from genm-sj5-schur, plus my reading of the skeleton, has clarified the honest scope of the §5 lane — worth your awareness because it corrects an over-optimistic framing from a few updates ago ("just finish the reshape (b2) and g(Q) closes"). **What schur found:** building the reshape toward the (3,3,3,4) q=2 target, the front-first brick g(Q) = ∫frobSq(A₀·Q)^{−c'} — closed via the spectral lower bound + a per-block radial blow-up of A₀'s *front* columns — provably **undershoots** the threshold (it reaches 3, not the required 7/2). The missing 7/2−3 is the **deep-layer** Jacobian: the corner units are deep data (‖w·A₂‖²), and the extra charge accumulates *across* the peel layers, which the front-only blow-up cannot see. **What the skeleton says (my read this tick):** the outer proof was never meant to close via a self-contained g(Q). It peels the front and reduces to an inner integral whose intended fill **recurses** — it invokes the induction hypothesis on the one-shorter chain at a threshold shifted by the front peel's charge (local peel carries part, the recursion carries the rest, summing to 7/2). So schur's front-first brick undershoots precisely *because it bypasses the recursion*; the proper fill is the recursive **(S,J) descent** the skeleton already isolates as its one open hole. **Net for you:** (i) not a wall, not a soundness problem — the result is true and the architecture is sound; it's a *scope* correction. (ii) The g(Q) machinery we've banked (the two per-cell finiteness bricks + the blow-up atom + the spectral bound) is **not wasted** — it's almost certainly the *terminal* of the descent (the innermost monomial-finiteness step); what's missing is the descent that connects the front peel to that terminal through the recursion. (iii) The honest remaining §5 content is that (S,J) descent — the deepest machinery, a substantial fresh build — not a quick reshape finish. This vindicates the "confirm the front-first route actually fills the hole" seam-check I flagged (#107 residual). I'm being deliberate here rather than racing to commission the build: spinning up a decorrelated scoping pass (pen-and-paper + Codex) to nail the descent's build-plan and confirm the banked bricks are the terminal *before* formalising, exactly per "pen-and-paper the math Lean-friendly BEFORE formalising." No decision needed from you unless you want to weigh in on scope; flagging so the ETA picture is straight.
expeditions/2026-06-20-aoyagi-full/discuss-at-close.md:2969:Per your scheduling note, I reorganized the (□) endgame from the serial D→F→base chain into parallel worktree lanes (Base-Cayley front-loaded, plus D-A, F, the D-C corollary, and an off-critical-path eigen-coordinate Mathlib-gap scout), pre-staged the #108 mint wiring (verified end-to-end: `DecoratedDescent → driver → (□) → unconditional headline` typechecks green), and built a durable interface tracker (`endgame-lanes.md`) since the parallel builds need tight interface discipline. **The notable outcome:** both #156 base-case tides, at their mandatory pre-build checkpoint, INDEPENDENTLY found that the 3-width base-case finiteness is *already proved* — `routeMBoxThresholdFinite_mnp` (unconditional over all widths, clean-three, and already the load-bearing R1-UPPER atom of our L2 interface). I verified it myself (faithful reshape to the box integral, threshold `= ½·minAdm` by `rfl`, no waist-excluding hypothesis, no `sorry`). So the whole SVD/Cayley waist construction the certs had scoped — a heavy build resting on an eigenvalue-density result Mathlib lacks — was **redundant**: the certs designed it without knowing `_mnp` closed the waist via a different banked route (a radial-Schur recursion). **What this means for you, plainly:** two lanes stood down with zero wasted Lean, the endgame is one genuine brick lighter than believed, and the "audit banked work before re-deriving" discipline (same family as the earlier Wall-C over-scope) paid off exactly as intended — decorrelated tides + a controller verify caught it at the checkpoint. No decision pending. The residual it leaves is item #137.
