expeditions/2026-06-20-aoyagi-full/threads/31-pin2-comparability/codex/l2wire-hptri-route-answer.md:9:This is **not true from the stated facts**. Reason: if both left frames send the same deepest layer to the same corner, then `Pf0 = U · P0'` with `U = [[I, *], [0, *]]`; dually `Qf1 = Q1' · V` with `V = [[I, 0], [*, *]]`. These are precisely the non-triangular directions that can change the `(2,2)` Schur complement of a general residual. The obstruction is leakage through the free `U12` and `V21` blocks. Normalising the deepest point only fixes the action on the corner matrix, not the Schur complement of nearby residuals.
