expeditions/2026-07-17-aoyagi-engine/threads/02-covdesign/codex/coverage-design-answer.md:15:and a support-preserving calculation must identify every \(U_i\) with exactly one stated child, including mixed exceptional factors. “Divisible by \(u\)” must mean divisibility in the local coordinate ring, not a pointwise condition. [proof-sketch you can defend] Outside the center the blow-up is an isomorphism, while over it the \(U_i\) cover the projective exceptional fibre; induction over the finite tree then gives global coverage. Properness supplies compact preimages and finite subcovers, but does not establish the child formulas or their exhaustiveness.
